diff --git a/plugin/plugins/game_agent_minecraft/docs/2026-10-11-query-progress-repair.md b/plugin/plugins/game_agent_minecraft/docs/2026-10-11-query-progress-repair.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..daa1770
--- /dev/null
+++ b/plugin/plugins/game_agent_minecraft/docs/2026-10-11-query-progress-repair.md
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Separate query feedback from execution progress
+
+The reported symptom was repeated wheat-harvesting narration while the body
+stayed near the same village position. Read-only observations covered a
+32-second unchanged interval and the longer vitals history. Fresh narration
+IDs and tool-cap exits accompanied repeated catalogue/status queries. This is
+evidence of newly generated planning, not proof of a replayed TTS file.
+
+Two input/scheduling failures were reproduced:
+
+- Solicited query replies were excluded from immediate attention callbacks but
+  still changed the revision used by idle retry backoff. Changing catalogue
+  records could also reset that revision without physical or quest progress.
+- A browsed `MC_MARKET_DETAIL` without `currentStep` became the focused task.
+  The actual `/mycli guild status` reply described a different accepted quest;
+  the short event/history buffers discarded it after unrelated queries.
+
+Solicited system/title/protection feedback remains readable, but does not
+reset idle backoff. Unsolicited protection failures, real chat/whispers and
+`MC_MARKET_CHECK` progress still change decisions. Unaccepted catalogue detail
+is now `serverPlay.inspectedReference`, separate from an actual active report.
+The latest real guild-status reply is retained for at most ten minutes, with
+its age, within its game session. It is historical server text, not a task
+acceptance inferred by the plugin or authorization to act.
+
+The change does not shorten the existing retry timer, suppress speech by text
+matching, remove game evidence, or issue escape actions. The matching native
+repair prevents an advisory legacy night-shelter commitment from cancelling
+another task's path. It retains an executing nightShelter's deliberate hold.
+
+Regression scenarios cover repeated solicited feedback, actual progress,
+private messages, unsolicited denials, session/age boundaries and 400/700-token
+capsules. A fake-clock service test verifies that two-second query feedback
+does not turn the existing 30/60-second retry schedule into a wakeup loop.
+Live verification must separately inspect accepted actions, position changes,
+task results and remaining repetition; passing these tests is not completion
+of the wheat quest or evidence that every physical trap can be escaped.
